<div class="system-diagrams">
<figure class="system-plate system-plate--stellar">
  <div class="orbit-plate" role="img" aria-label="Top-down schematic of the close binary Maia A and Maia B, four small inner circumbinary planets, and the remote red dwarf Maia C on a much larger eccentric orbit">
    <div class="orbit-plate__system" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="stellar-orbit"></div>
      <div class="planetary-orbit planetary-orbit--iv"><span class="system-planet system-planet--iv"></span></div>
      <div class="planetary-orbit planetary-orbit--iii"><span class="system-planet system-planet--iii"></span></div>
      <div class="planetary-orbit planetary-orbit--ii"><span class="system-planet system-planet--ii"></span></div>
      <div class="planetary-orbit planetary-orbit--i"><span class="system-planet system-planet--i"></span></div>
      <div class="binary-orbit"></div>
      <span class="star star--a"></span>
      <span class="star star--b"></span>
      <span class="star star--c"></span>
    </div>

  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span>01 · Stellar architecture</span>
    <p>Maia A and Maia B form the close central binary. Maia I through Maia IV follow inner circumbinary paths; Maia C is the distant third light on a much larger eccentric stellar path whose closest approach remains well beyond Maia IV. This diagram specifically omits Maia V through Maia XII, which occupy the system’s farther reaches. Relative sizes, distances, and eccentricity are diagrammatic.</p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<figure class="system-plate system-plate--lunar">
  <div class="lunar-plate" role="img" aria-label="Separate local diagram of Maia IV with Clotho, Lachesis, and Atropos on three widely separated satellite orbits">
    <div class="moon-system" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="moon-orbit moon-orbit--atropos"><span class="moon moon--atropos"></span></div>
      <div class="moon-orbit moon-orbit--lachesis"><span class="moon moon--lachesis"></span></div>
      <div class="moon-orbit moon-orbit--clotho"><span class="moon moon--clotho"></span></div>
      <span class="planet planet--inset"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span>02 · Maia IV satellite system</span>
    <p>Clotho, Lachesis, and Atropos occupy three distinct, well-separated orbital tracks. This local view is a second schematic—not an enlargement held to the stellar diagram’s scale.</p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
